W — Use of Switch: 9/10; Technical execution: 9/10; Creativity and impact: 8/10; Presentation and documentation: 9/10. Weighted total: 8.75/10. Strong evidence of a working Switch-centered workflow, careful approval controls, and clear reproduction steps. The idea is useful, though its impact is shown on synthetic data.

Y — Use of Switch: 9/10; Technical execution: 8/10; Creativity and impact: 8/10; Presentation and documentation: 7/10. Weighted total: 8.10/10. A substantial, tested workflow with a clear human approval gate. The missing demo video leaves a key presentation requirement unfulfilled.

Z — Use of Switch: 8/10; Technical execution: 7/10; Creativity and impact: 9/10; Presentation and documentation: 7/10. Weighted total: 7.75/10. Testing business rules with generated exploits is compelling, but some listed capabilities remain planned, and the local stack has not been run.

X — Use of Switch: 9/10; Technical execution: 2/10; Creativity and impact: 9/10; Presentation and documentation: 6/10. Weighted total: 6.15/10. The privacy-preserving cross-team review concept is original and makes strong use of Switch permissions, but the core product and demo are explicitly not built.

W ranks first because it pairs a live, evidenced Switch workflow with reproducible instructions; Y is second with a broader tested tool, but no demo video.

RANK: WYZX